<div class="markup-toc-wrapper">
<button class="markup-toc-button">Show Table of Contents</button></div>Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Feral Druid DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 4. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Dragon Soul, Firelands, Twilight Protocol Dungeons, and Valor Points. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c11">Best in Slot Gear for Feral Druid DPS in  Phase 4</span></h2>Feral Druid DPS secondary stats are almost all identical in value and your main goal in gearing as Feral Druid DPS is to get as much Agility as possible, meaning item level is king. The list below is the priority in full BiS, Expertise/<wbr/>Critical Strike/<wbr/>Mastery all jump up and down in value depending on what you have on your gear already, but are always almost identical. Haste is the only secondary stat that is consistently the worst, but that is assuming a perfect rotation where you fill a lot of your time waiting for Energy by <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve#advanced-tips-and-tricks">"weaving"</a>.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Agility - You want as much Agility as possible. Look to fill any gem slot with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71879/delicate-queens-garnet">
<img alt="Delicate Queen's Garnet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_epicgem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Queen's Garnet</span></a> the only exception being if an equal amount of Agility is gained by matching a socket or if the gain in secondary stats is 3× more than the loss in Agility.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - Hit Rating until the cap of 8% will always be the best secondary stat for Feral Druid DPS</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - Expertise Rating until the soft-cap of 6.5% is not going to be a problem in Dragon Soul due to a lot of Expertise Rating on gear, it is likely you will be worried about getting too much Expertise.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Critical Strike Rating is your strongest secondary stat that can not reach a cap, making it the stat that you ideally would want on every piece of gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Mastery Rating is very similar to Critical Strike Rating, but in full BiS setup, it falls just behind. Another important factor for Mastery is that it does not scale with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=62078/swipe">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_monsterclaw_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Swipe</span></a>, meaning that it loses a lot of value on big AOE, but on the other hand, it scales well with cleave through multi-dotting your bleeds.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Haste Rating falls behind for Feral Druid DPS compared to other secondary stats, due to being able to fill your globals through <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/druid/feral/dps-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve#advanced-tips-and-tricks">"weaving"</a>. However, if you decide not to weave, Haste becomes on par with Critical Strike and Mastery, where it depends on your current gear setup which is better, but they're all almost identical.</div></li></ol>
